<title>GERMANY: AHB plans 1 bln dmk Pfandbrief Tuesday.</title>
<headline>AHB plans 1 bln dmk Pfandbrief Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allgemeine Hypothekenbank AG (AHB) plans to issue a one billion-mark Jumbo Pfandbrief bond with a coupon of 3.50 percent on Tuesday, the lead managers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bond matures in January 13 2000, and the spread over the Series 113 Bundesobligationen, or Bobl, bonds will be seven basis points, Dresdner said.</p>
<p>The pay date is May 13 1997. Terms will be announced on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Lead managers are CSFB, Commerzbank AG, Deutsche Bank and Dresdner Bank.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
